    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-20-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-20-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(3) A review under subsection (1) is to be conducted by a person who\nhas expertise in:\n\n(a) competition law; and\n\n(b) economics.\n\n(4) A review under subsection (1) must make provision for public\nconsultation.\n\n(5) The Minister must cause to be prepared a report of a review under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(6) The Minister must ensure that the report is completed within 6\nmonths after the end of the 2-year period mentioned in\nsubsection (1).\n\n(7) The Minister must cause copies of the report to be tabled in each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe completion of the preparation of the report.",
      "skos:definition": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(3) A review under subsection (1) is to be conducted by a person who\nhas expertise in:\n\n(a) competition law; and\n\n(b) economics.\n\n(4) A review under subsection (1) must make provision for public\nconsultation.\n\n(5) The Minister must cause to be prepared a report of a review under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(6) The Minister must ensure that the report is completed within 6\nmonths after the end of the 2-year period mentioned in\nsubsection (1).\n\n(7) The Minister must cause copies of the report to be tabled in each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe completion of the preparation of the report.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-20-2-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-20-2-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-20-2-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-20-2-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-20-2-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bc806b2c26ce22cd25c65c81147bd806a1f45bd04468bfcf1248ff1791822f94"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-20-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(3) A review under subsection (1) is to be conducted by a person who\nhas expertise in:\n\n(a) competition law; and\n\n(b) economics.\n\n(4) A review under subsection (1) must make provision for public\nconsultation.\n\n(5) The Minister must cause to be prepared a report of a review under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(6) The Minister must ensure that the report is completed within 6\nmonths after the end of the 2-year period mentioned in\nsubsection (1).\n\n(7) The Minister must cause copies of the report to be tabled in each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe completion of the preparation of the report."
    },
