      "skos:note": "NBN corporation must not discriminate in favour of itself Grounds for believing access seeker is not creditworthy or has failed to comply with terms and conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28(7) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(7) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in\nparagraph (6)(a) include:\n\n(a) evidence that the access seeker is not creditworthy; and\n\n(b) repeated failures by the access seeker to comply with the\nterms and conditions on which the same or similar access has\nbeen provided (whether or not by the NBN corporation).\nDefinition"
    },
