      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The rule in subsection (1) does not prevent discrimination against\nan access seeker if the NBN corporation has reasonable grounds to\nbelieve that the access seeker would fail, to a material extent, to\ncomply with the terms and conditions on which the NBN\ncorporation complies, or on which the NBN corporation is\nreasonably likely to comply, with the relevant obligation.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The rule in subsection (1) does not prevent discrimination against\nan access seeker if the NBN corporation has reasonable grounds to\nbelieve that the access seeker would fail, to a material extent, to\ncomply with the terms and conditions on which the NBN\ncorporation complies, or on which the NBN corporation is\nreasonably likely to comply, with the relevant obligation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
