        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "NBN corporation has reasonable grounds to believe access seeker would fail to comply with terms and conditions",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Discrimination is recurrent if NBN corporation believes access seeker will comply with terms and conditions under certain circumstances"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28(3) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in subsection (2)\ninclude:\n\n(a) evidence that the access seeker is not creditworthy; and\n\n(b) repeated failures by the access seeker to comply with the\nterms and conditions on which the same or similar access has\nbeen provided (whether or not by the NBN corporation).\nNo discrimination by an NBN corporation in favour of itself",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in subsection (2)\ninclude:\n\n(a) evidence that the access seeker is not creditworthy; and\n\n(b) repeated failures by the access seeker to comply with the\nterms and conditions on which the same or similar access has\nbeen provided (whether or not by the NBN corporation).\nNo discrimination by an NBN corporation in favour of itself",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5fac43ab58de3e112761ffa85916b0477b6618987d33623e4066c516cfc5d16a",
      "skos:note": "No discrimination by NBN corporation in favour of itself"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28(3) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in subsection (2)\ninclude:\n\n(a) evidence that the access seeker is not creditworthy; and\n\n(b) repeated failures by the access seeker to comply with the\nterms and conditions on which the same or similar access has\nbeen provided (whether or not by the NBN corporation).\nNo discrimination by an NBN corporation in favour of itself"
    },
    {
