        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-7-logic-deontic-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-7-logic-alleninterval-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-7-logic-ltl-8"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-7-logic-diffusion-9"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-7-logic-cogai-10"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a9c9956c2fe543c8688f539d62f848d763f2cef743155ffd0c0103a86d2cf24b",
      "skos:note": "NBN corporation must not discriminate in favour of itself Grounds for believing access seeker is not creditworthy or has failed to comply with terms and conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-28-2-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28(7) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If:\n\n(a) an NBN corporation is a carrier or carriage service provider;\nand\n\n(b) under subsection 152AL(8A), (8D) or (8E), a declared\nservice relates to the NBN corporation; and\n\n(c) the NBN corporation is subject to a category B standard\naccess obligation in relation to the service;\nthe NBN corporation must not discriminate in favour of itself in\nrelation to the supply of the service.\nAuthorised conduct"
    },
