      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1AB) If the Federal Court is satisfied that an NBN corporation has\ncontravened the rule in subsection 152AXC(1) or (7) or\n152AXD(1), the Court may, on the application of:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          31\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the NBN corporation to comply with that\nrule;\n\n(d) an order directing the NBN corporation to compensate any\nother person who had suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1AB) If the Federal Court is satisfied that an NBN corporation has\ncontravened the rule in subsection 152AXC(1) or (7) or\n152AXD(1), the Court may, on the application of:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          31\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the NBN corporation to comply with that\nrule;\n\n(d) an order directing the NBN corporation to compensate any\nother person who had suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-53-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-53-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "42a09cba4db67e772735d9bc19817c594b645d44ebc30afb18a41edc1fff34b4",
      "skos:note": "Court may make orders to comply with rule or compensate affected persons"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 After subsection 152BB(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1AB) If the Federal Court is satisfied that an NBN corporation has\ncontravened the rule in subsection 152AXC(1) or (7) or\n152AXD(1), the Court may, on the application of:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          31\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the NBN corporation to comply with that\nrule;\n\n(d) an order directing the NBN corporation to compensate any\nother person who had suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate."
    },
