      "cml:integrityHash": "10cf0abb63a7b1cd17a8f86a8128b83552391acd7775c34dcc1334bfacc38411",
      "skos:note": "Commission may remove material from statement in Register if it prejudices substantially commercial interests and outweighs public interest."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40(5) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the Commission is satisfied that:\n\n(a) publication of particular material contained in a statement\ncould reasonably be expected to prejudice substantially the\ncommercial interests of a person; and\n\n(b) the prejudice outweighs the public interest in the publication\nof the matter;\nthe Commission may remove the material from the version of the\nstatement that is included in the Register."
