    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46(1) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that an NBN corporation has\ncontravened an obligation imposed by section 152CJA or 152CJB,\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the NBN corporation to comply with the\nobligation;\n\n(d) an order directing the NBN corporation to compensate any\nother person who has suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that an NBN corporation has\ncontravened an obligation imposed by section 152CJA or 152CJB,\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the NBN corporation to comply with the\nobligation;\n\n(d) an order directing the NBN corporation to compensate any\nother person who has suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-46-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5e1869a3fbf44e8e9dd6df80e9de08bc8885693aa9aa47aaeababa93cc56410",
      "skos:note": "Court may order NBN corporation to comply with obligation or compensate affected persons. Service provider rule for the purposes of the Telecommunications Act 1997."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46(1) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that an NBN corporation has\ncontravened an obligation imposed by section 152CJA or 152CJB,\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the NBN corporation to comply with the\nobligation;\n\n(d) an order directing the NBN corporation to compensate any\nother person who has suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate."
    },
