      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-142a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "142A Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-142a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\nalter, in relation to a telecommunications network, has a meaning\naffected by section 159.\nelectricity supply body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part:\nalter, in relation to a telecommunications network, has a meaning\naffected by section 159.\nelectricity supply body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-142a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1bdeba30fd37aa16acce9ded89b7f9a470f7b1c2e818a991cb230d1c3c63daa4",
      "skos:note": "Definition of 'alter' in relation to a telecommunications network"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-142a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "142A Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\nalter, in relation to a telecommunications network, has a meaning\naffected by section 159.\nelectricity supply body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-142a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-142a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-60-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-60-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\neligible service has the same meaning as in section 152AL of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010.\ngas supply body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nlocal access line has the meaning given by section 158.\nnational broadband network has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nrail corporation has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsewerage services body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsmall business customer means:\n\n(a) a customer who is a small business employer (within the\nmeaning of the Fair Work Act 2009); or\n\n(b) a customer who:\n\n(i) carries on a business; and\n\n(ii) does not have any employees.\nFor the purposes of paragraph (a) of this definition, it is to be\nassumed that each reference in section 23 of the Fair Work Act\n2009 to a national system employer were a reference to an\nemployer (within the ordinary meaning of that expression).\nState or Territory road authority has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nstorm water drainage services has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nstorm water drainage services body has the same meaning as in\nthe National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsuperfast carriage service means a carriage service, where:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the download transmission speed of the carriage service is\nnormally more than 25 megabits per second; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          61\n\n(c) the carriage service is supplied using a line to premises\noccupied or used by an end-user.\nupgrade, in relation to a telecommunications network, has a\nmeaning affected by section 160.\nwater supply body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.",
      "skos:definition": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\neligible service has the same meaning as in section 152AL of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010.\ngas supply body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nlocal access line has the meaning given by section 158.\nnational broadband network has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nrail corporation has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsewerage services body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsmall business customer means:\n\n(a) a customer who is a small business employer (within the\nmeaning of the Fair Work Act 2009); or\n\n(b) a customer who:\n\n(i) carries on a business; and\n\n(ii) does not have any employees.\nFor the purposes of paragraph (a) of this definition, it is to be\nassumed that each reference in section 23 of the Fair Work Act\n2009 to a national system employer were a reference to an\nemployer (within the ordinary meaning of that expression).\nState or Territory road authority has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nstorm water drainage services has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nstorm water drainage services body has the same meaning as in\nthe National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsuperfast carriage service means a carriage service, where:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the download transmission speed of the carriage service is\nnormally more than 25 megabits per second; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          61\n\n(c) the carriage service is supplied using a line to premises\noccupied or used by an end-user.\nupgrade, in relation ",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-60-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-60-2-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-60-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0203432c2a47456393ec59be13f13d1cebad3c4b75fc4669936b4b6f0cca0796",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms used in telecommunications legislation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-60-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\neligible service has the same meaning as in section 152AL of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010.\ngas supply body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nlocal access line has the meaning given by section 158.\nnational broadband network has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nrail corporation has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsewerage services body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsmall business customer means:\n\n(a) a customer who is a small business employer (within the\nmeaning of the Fair Work Act 2009); or\n\n(b) a customer who:\n\n(i) carries on a business; and\n\n(ii) does not have any employees.\nFor the purposes of paragraph (a) of this definition, it is to be\nassumed that each reference in section 23 of the Fair Work Act\n2009 to a national system employer were a reference to an\nemployer (within the ordinary meaning of that expression).\nState or Territory road authority has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nstorm water drainage services has the same meaning as in the\nNational Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nstorm water drainage services body has the same meaning as in\nthe National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011.\nsuperfast carriage service means a carriage service, where:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the download transmission speed of the carriage service is\nnormally more than 25 megabits per second; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          61\n\n(c) the carriage service is supplied using a line to premises\noccupied or used by an end-user.\nupgrade, in relation to a telecommunications network, has a\nmeaning affected by section 160.\nwater supply body has the same meaning as in the National\nBroadband Network Companies Act 2011."
    },
