    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-62-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "62 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-62-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\npersons, to supply an eligible service unless the service is supplied\nto:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a service provider.\nNote 1:\nFor when a person is in a position to exercise control of a network, see\nsection 155.\nNote 2:\nFor control of a company, see section 154.\nOffence\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection (2);\nand\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty: 20,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\npersons, to supply an eligible service unless the service is supplied\nto:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a service provider.\nNote 1:\nFor when a person is in a position to exercise control of a network, see\nsection 155.\nNote 2:\nFor control of a company, see section 154.\nOffence\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection (2);\nand\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty: 20,000 penalty units.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-62-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-62-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-62-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-62-2-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-62-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-62-2-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "651b2c5551fcecfda37abe6b775b438835a915a162e4471a6f43cf38710a4f85",
      "skos:note": "No person shall supply an eligible service unless the service is supplied to a carrier or a service provider."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-62-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "62 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\npersons, to supply an eligible service unless the service is supplied\nto:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a service provider.\nNote 1:\nFor when a person is in a position to exercise control of a network, see\nsection 155.\nNote 2:\nFor control of a company, see section 154.\nOffence\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection (2);\nand\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty: 20,000 penalty units."
    },
