    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-64-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-64-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(ii) the sole use of the carriage service is use by a rail\ncorporation to carry communications necessary or\ndesirable for the workings of train services; or\n\n(b) the eligible service is a service that facilitates the supply of a\ncarriage service covered by paragraph (a) of this subsection.\n\n(6) Paragraph (5)(a) does not apply to a carriage service supplied to a\nrail corporation unless the carriage service is supplied on the basis\nthat the rail corporation must not re-supply the carriage service.",
      "skos:definition": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(ii) the sole use of the carriage service is use by a rail\ncorporation to carry communications necessary or\ndesirable for the workings of train services; or\n\n(b) the eligible service is a service that facilitates the supply of a\ncarriage service covered by paragraph (a) of this subsection.\n\n(6) Paragraph (5)(a) does not apply to a carriage service supplied to a\nrail corporation unless the carriage service is supplied on the basis\nthat the rail corporation must not re-supply the carriage service.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-64-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-64-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f44535b19bbe42adf14f160585cdd9ad04cf5160ba82bc57109033aa074bb131",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on re-supply of carriage service to rail corporation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-64-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "64 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(ii) the sole use of the carriage service is use by a rail\ncorporation to carry communications necessary or\ndesirable for the workings of train services; or\n\n(b) the eligible service is a service that facilitates the supply of a\ncarriage service covered by paragraph (a) of this subsection.\n\n(6) Paragraph (5)(a) does not apply to a carriage service supplied to a\nrail corporation unless the carriage service is supplied on the basis\nthat the rail corporation must not re-supply the carriage service."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-64-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
