    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-70-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-70-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, if:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network is extended on or after",
      "skos:definition": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, if:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network is extended on or after",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-70-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "489559b934f782e6dd24e358f85a8d02ab49a4dbc7c41ac352d18efec351830b",
      "skos:note": "Conditional commencement for telecommunications network extension"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-70-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "70 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, if:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network is extended on or after"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-70-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-70-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-1-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 January 2011; and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-1-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(b) the extended part of the network is capable of being used to\nsupply a superfast carriage service to residential or small\nbusiness customers, or prospective residential or small\nbusiness customers, in Australia;\nthen:\n\n(c) the extended part is taken to be a network in its own right;\nand\n\n(d) the network referred to in paragraph (c) is taken to have come\ninto existence on or after 1 January 2011.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a part of the infrastructure of a telecommunications network\nis situated in a particular area that is being or was developed\nas a particular stage of a real estate development project\n(within the ordinary meaning of that expression); and\n\n(b) the network is extended to another area that is being, or is to\nbe, developed as another stage of the project;\nsubsection (2) does not apply to the extension.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network was in existence immediately\nbefore 1 January 2011; and\n\n(b) the network is extended on or after 1 January 2011; and\n\n(c) no point on the infrastructure of the extension is located more\nthan:\n\n(i) 1 kilometre; or\n\n(ii) if a longer distance is specified in the regulations—that\nlonger distance;\n\nfrom a point on the infrastructure of the network as the\nnetwork stood immediately before 1 January 2011;\nsubsection (2) does not apply to the extension.\n\n(5) The regulations may provide that subsection (2) does not apply to a\nspecified extension of a telecommunications network.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          71",
      "skos:definition": "(b) the extended part of the network is capable of being used to\nsupply a superfast carriage service to residential or small\nbusiness customers, or prospective residential or small\nbusiness customers, in Australia;\nthen:\n\n(c) the extended part is taken to be a network in its own right;\nand\n\n(d) the network referred to in paragraph (c) is taken to have come\ninto existence on or after 1 January 2011.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a part of the infrastructure of a telecommunications network\nis situated in a particular area that is being or was developed\nas a particular stage of a real estate development project\n(within the ordinary meaning of that expression); and\n\n(b) the network is extended to another area that is being, or is to\nbe, developed as another stage of the project;\nsubsection (2) does not apply to the extension.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network was in existence immediately\nbefore 1 January 2011; and\n\n(b) the network is extended on or after 1 January 2011; and\n\n(c) no point on the infrastructure of the extension is located more\nthan:\n\n(i) 1 kilometre; or\n\n(ii) if a longer distance is specified in the regulations—that\nlonger distance;\n\nfrom a point on the infrastructure of the network as the\nnetwork stood immediately before 1 January 2011;\nsubsection (2) does not apply to the extension.\n\n(5) The regulations may provide that subsection (2) does not apply to a\nspecified extension of a telecommunications network.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          71",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-1-7-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-1-7-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-1-7-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "440c43ffab4be110e69e9a772f56d052246c01af01bf165b06be83fe24bd04e1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-1-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 January 2011; and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(b) the extended part of the network is capable of being used to\nsupply a superfast carriage service to residential or small\nbusiness customers, or prospective residential or small\nbusiness customers, in Australia;\nthen:\n\n(c) the extended part is taken to be a network in its own right;\nand\n\n(d) the network referred to in paragraph (c) is taken to have come\ninto existence on or after 1 January 2011.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a part of the infrastructure of a telecommunications network\nis situated in a particular area that is being or was developed\nas a particular stage of a real estate development project\n(within the ordinary meaning of that expression); and\n\n(b) the network is extended to another area that is being, or is to\nbe, developed as another stage of the project;\nsubsection (2) does not apply to the extension.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network was in existence immediately\nbefore 1 January 2011; and\n\n(b) the network is extended on or after 1 January 2011; and\n\n(c) no point on the infrastructure of the extension is located more\nthan:\n\n(i) 1 kilometre; or\n\n(ii) if a longer distance is specified in the regulations—that\nlonger distance;\n\nfrom a point on the infrastructure of the network as the\nnetwork stood immediately before 1 January 2011;\nsubsection (2) does not apply to the extension.\n\n(5) The regulations may provide that subsection (2) does not apply to a\nspecified extension of a telecommunications network.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          71"
    },
