    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-80-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80(2) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-80-2-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The carrier or provider must not, in carrying on any of the\nfollowing activities, discriminate between access seekers:\n\n(a) developing a new eligible service;\n\n(b) enhancing a declared service;\n\n(c) extending or enhancing the capability of a facility or\ntelecommunications network by means of which a declared\nservice is, or is to be, supplied;\n\n(d) planning for a facility or telecommunications network by\nmeans of which a declared service is, or is to be, supplied;\n\n(e) an activity that is preparatory to the supply of a declared\nservice;\n\n(f) an activity that is ancillary or incidental to the supply of a\ndeclared service;\n\n(g) giving information to service providers about any of the\nabove activities.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH.\nDefinition",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The carrier or provider must not, in carrying on any of the\nfollowing activities, discriminate between access seekers:\n\n(a) developing a new eligible service;\n\n(b) enhancing a declared service;\n\n(c) extending or enhancing the capability of a facility or\ntelecommunications network by means of which a declared\nservice is, or is to be, supplied;\n\n(d) planning for a facility or telecommunications network by\nmeans of which a declared service is, or is to be, supplied;\n\n(e) an activity that is preparatory to the supply of a declared\nservice;\n\n(f) an activity that is ancillary or incidental to the supply of a\ndeclared service;\n\n(g) giving information to service providers about any of the\nabove activities.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH.\nDefinition",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-80-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-80-2-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-80-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e63bcf2770dd57dfa823872eff3b17176476de863f183266ef9ae084144d4850",
      "skos:note": "Discrimination between access seekers is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-80-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80(2) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The carrier or provider must not, in carrying on any of the\nfollowing activities, discriminate between access seekers:\n\n(a) developing a new eligible service;\n\n(b) enhancing a declared service;\n\n(c) extending or enhancing the capability of a facility or\ntelecommunications network by means of which a declared\nservice is, or is to be, supplied;\n\n(d) planning for a facility or telecommunications network by\nmeans of which a declared service is, or is to be, supplied;\n\n(e) an activity that is preparatory to the supply of a declared\nservice;\n\n(f) an activity that is ancillary or incidental to the supply of a\ndeclared service;\n\n(g) giving information to service providers about any of the\nabove activities.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH.\nDefinition"
    },
