    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-82-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "82 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-82-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(1AA) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a carrier or carriage service\nprovider has contravened the rule in subsection 152ARA(1) or (7)\nor 152ARB(2), the Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the carrier or provider to comply with the\nobligation;\n\n(d) an order directing the carrier or provider to compensate any\nother person who had suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(1AA) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a carrier or carriage service\nprovider has contravened the rule in subsection 152ARA(1) or (7)\nor 152ARB(2), the Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the carrier or provider to comply with the\nobligation;\n\n(d) an order directing the carrier or provider to compensate any\nother person who had suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-82-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-82-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c392756b6d96d6d0f822cd0a56236e350b6b767ca0d5ee94c992ae671fdbe7b6",
      "skos:note": "Carrier or carriage service provider must comply with the rule."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-82-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "82 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "Network Measures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011\n\n(1AA) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a carrier or carriage service\nprovider has contravened the rule in subsection 152ARA(1) or (7)\nor 152ARB(2), the Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(c) an order directing the carrier or provider to comply with the\nobligation;\n\n(d) an order directing the carrier or provider to compensate any\nother person who had suffered loss or damage as a result of\nthe contravention;\n\n(e) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate."
    },
    {
