      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-104",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "104 Before subsection 152BCB(5)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-104"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(4G) The Commission must not make an access determination that:\n\n(a) relates to a declared service that is:\n\n(i) a Layer 2 bitstream service; and\n\n(ii) supplied using a designated superfast\ntelecommunications network; and\n\n(iii) supplied by a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) or\na carriage service provider (other than an NBN\ncorporation); and\n\n(b) has the effect (whether direct or indirect) of discriminating\nbetween access seekers.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH.\n\n(4H) Subsection (4G) does not prevent discrimination against an access\nseeker if the Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that\nthe access seeker would fail, to a material extent, to comply with\nthe terms and conditions on which the carrier or carriage service\nprovider complies, or on which the carrier or carriage service\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          83\nprovider is reasonably likely to comply, with the relevant\nobligation.\n\n(4J) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in\nsubsection (4H) include:\n\n(a) evidence that the access seeker is not creditworthy; and\n\n(b) repeated failures by the access seeker to comply with the\nterms and conditions on which the same or similar access has\nbeen provided (whether or not by the carrier or carriage\nservice provider).",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(4G) The Commission must not make an access determination that:\n\n(a) relates to a declared service that is:\n\n(i) a Layer 2 bitstream service; and\n\n(ii) supplied using a designated superfast\ntelecommunications network; and\n\n(iii) supplied by a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) or\na carriage service provider (other than an NBN\ncorporation); and\n\n(b) has the effect (whether direct or indirect) of discriminating\nbetween access seekers.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH.\n\n(4H) Subsection (4G) does not prevent discrimination against an access\nseeker if the Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that\nthe access seeker would fail, to a material extent, to comply with\nthe terms and conditions on which the carrier or carriage service\nprovider complies, or on which the carrier or carriage service\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          83\nprovider is reasonably likely to comply, with the relevant\nobligation.\n\n(4J) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in\nsubsection (4H) include:\n\n(a) evidence that the access seeker is not creditworthy; and\n\n(b) repeated failures by the access seeker to comply with the\nterms and conditions on which the same or similar access has\nbeen provided (whether or not by the carrier or carriage\nservice provider).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-104-ss-4g"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-104-ss-4h"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-104-ss-4j"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-104",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "104 Before subsection 152BCB(5)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(4G) The Commission must not make an access determination that:\n\n(a) relates to a declared service that is:\n\n(i) a Layer 2 bitstream service; and\n\n(ii) supplied using a designated superfast\ntelecommunications network; and\n\n(iii) supplied by a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) or\na carriage service provider (other than an NBN\ncorporation); and\n\n(b) has the effect (whether direct or indirect) of discriminating\nbetween access seekers.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH.\n\n(4H) Subsection (4G) does not prevent discrimination against an access\nseeker if the Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that\nthe access seeker would fail, to a material extent, to comply with\nthe terms and conditions on which the carrier or carriage service\nprovider complies, or on which the carrier or carriage service\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00870\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments relating to Layer 2 bitstream services  Part 3\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (National Broadband Network\nMeasures—Access Arrangements) Act 2011          83\nprovider is reasonably likely to comply, with the relevant\nobligation.\n\n(4J) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in\nsubsection (4H) include:\n\n(a) evidence that the access seeker is not creditworthy; and\n\n(b) repeated failures by the access seeker to comply with the\nterms and conditions on which the same or similar access has\nbeen provided (whether or not by the carrier or carriage\nservice provider)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-104-ss-4g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "104(4G) Before subsection 152BCB(5)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-104-ss-4g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2012c00870.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2012c00870.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "(4G) The Commission must not make an access determination that:\n\n(a) relates to a declared service that is:\n\n(i) a Layer 2 bitstream service; and\n\n(ii) supplied using a designated superfast\ntelecommunications network; and\n\n(iii) supplied by a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) or\na carriage service provider (other than an NBN\ncorporation); and\n\n(b) has the effect (whether direct or indirect) of discriminating\nbetween access seekers.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH.",
      "skos:definition": "(4G) The Commission must not make an access determination that:\n\n(a) relates to a declared service that is:\n\n(i) a Layer 2 bitstream service; and\n\n(ii) supplied using a designated superfast\ntelecommunications network; and\n\n(iii) supplied by a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) or\na carriage service provider (other than an NBN\ncorporation); and\n\n(b) has the effect (whether direct or indirect) of discriminating\nbetween access seekers.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-104"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-104-ss-4g-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2012c00870-sch-1-sec-104-ss-4g-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2174a3098aaa4b63fdfa54c84fef6d94ab35930330513db46f4d3f9ddebb6a0c",
      "skos:note": "Commission must not make an access determination that discriminates between access seekers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2012c00870#sch-1-sec-104-ss-4g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "104(4G) Before subsection 152BCB(5)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "(4G) The Commission must not make an access determination that:\n\n(a) relates to a declared service that is:\n\n(i) a Layer 2 bitstream service; and\n\n(ii) supplied using a designated superfast\ntelecommunications network; and\n\n(iii) supplied by a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) or\na carriage service provider (other than an NBN\ncorporation); and\n\n(b) has the effect (whether direct or indirect) of discriminating\nbetween access seekers.\nNote:\nFor explanatory material, see section 152CJH."
    },
